<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Strong log-concavity and covariance bounds</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We repeatedly use the following standard consequences of
Bakry–Émery curvature. If a probability measure
<math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu(\mathrm{d}z)\propto e^{-W(z)}\,\mathrm{d}z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu(\mathrm{d}z)\propto e^{-W(z)}\,\mathrm{d}z</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies
<math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}W\succeq mI" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}W\succeq mI</annotation></semantics></math>, then, for smooth <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Var_{\nu}(f)\leq\frac{1}{m}\,\mathbb{E}_{\nu}\|\nabla f\|^{2}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">Var</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Var_{\nu}(f)\leq\frac{1}{m}\,\mathbb{E}_{\nu}\|\nabla f\|^{2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the log-Sobolev inequality with constant
<math id="A4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/m</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, every <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> obeys Gaussian
concentration</p>
<table id="A4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\{f-\mathbb{E}f\geq t\}\leq\exp\Bigl(-\frac{mt^{2}}{2L^{2}}\Bigr)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\{f-\mathbb{E}f\geq t\}\leq\exp\Bigl(-\frac{mt^{2}}{2L^{2}}\Bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">These statements follow from the Bakry–Émery criterion; see, for
example, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, Chapters 4 and 5]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Two-sided covariance bound)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu(\mathrm{d}z)\propto e^{-W(z)}\,\mathrm{d}z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu(\mathrm{d}z)\propto e^{-W(z)}\,\mathrm{d}z</annotation></semantics></math> with</span></p>
<table id="A4.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="mI\preceq\nabla^{2}W(z)\preceq LI\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">mI\preceq\nabla^{2}W(z)\preceq LI\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then</span></p>
<table id="A4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{-1}I\preceq\mathrm{Cov}_{\nu}(Z)\preceq m^{-1}I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{-1}I\preceq\mathrm{Cov}_{\nu}(Z)\preceq m^{-1}I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The upper bound is the Brascamp–Lieb
inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, Chapter 4]</cite> applied to linear functions. The lower
bound follows from the Cramér–Rao inequality for the location family
generated by <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}_{\nu}(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Cov}_{\nu}(Z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\succeq\bigl(\mathbb{E}_{\nu}\nabla^{2}W(Z)\bigr)^{-1}\succeq L^{-1}I\,.\qed" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⪰</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\succeq\bigl(\mathbb{E}_{\nu}\nabla^{2}W(Z)\bigr)^{-1}\succeq L^{-1}I\,.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Hessian of the augmented marginal.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{x}_{y}\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[X\mid Y=y]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{x}_{y}\coloneqq\mathbb{E}[X\mid Y=y]</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{y}\coloneqq\eta^{-1}\,\mathrm{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Cov</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{y}\coloneqq\eta^{-1}\,\mathrm{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)</annotation></semantics></math>, as in the normalized
coordinates of Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>. Differentiating the
log-density of <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}^{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}^{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla U_{\eta}(y)=\eta^{-1}(y-\bar{x}_{y})\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\nabla^{2}U_{\eta}(y)=\eta^{-1}(I-\Sigma_{y})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">¯</mo></mover><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla U_{\eta}(y)=\eta^{-1}(y-\bar{x}_{y})\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\nabla^{2}U_{\eta}(y)=\eta^{-1}(I-\Sigma_{y})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The conditional potential in <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> has Hessian between
<math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha+\eta^{-1})I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha+\eta^{-1})I</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta+\eta^{-1})I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta+\eta^{-1})I</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying
<a href="#A4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma D.3 (Two-sided covariance bound). ‣ D.2 Strong log-concavity and covariance bounds ‣ Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> in (<a href="#A4.E10" title="Equation D.10 ‣ Hessian of the augmented marginal. ‣ D.2 Strong log-concavity and covariance bounds ‣ Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.10</span></a>) gives
(<a href="#S2.E13" title="Equation 2.13 ‣ Item (ii) ‣ Proposition 2.1 (Geometry of the joint law). ‣ 2.2 Proximal augmentation and the restricted Gaussian oracle ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.13</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>